boot: stzos init -- machine makeen_box (hosted / aarch64 / rpi4) -- pid 1
boot: console /dev/ttyS1
boot: slots on /dev/mmcblk0p1 -- A and B
boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
boot: mount ext4 at /data -- done
boot: grant network (effectful)
boot: grant filesystem (effectful)
boot: refuse gpio (effectful)
boot: network lan -- eth0: no such interface (NODEV)
boot: slot B -- a trial (committed is A); the watchdog holds the rollback until every service has started
boot: watchdog -- off by the boot line (the emulator resets on arming); a trial cannot roll back by hardware here
boot: start kds -- pid N -- /stzr /app/kds.luau
kds: the kitchen display world is up on the Makeen box (aarch64, stzr under PID 1)
kds: read /etc/machine -- 8 declarations rode in the image
boot: kds (pid N) exited 0
boot: start poste -- pid N -- /stzr /app/poste.luau
poste: the counter world is up on the Makeen box, after kds
poste: /data is the box's persistent partition, mounted by PID 1 before any world spoke
boot: poste (pid N) exited 0
boot: slot B -- committed: every service is ready; config.txt now boots B, A is the fallback
boot: every service has ended -- init has nothing left to keep alive
boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
reboot: Restarting system
card: config.txt after the trial:
card: os_prefix=slots/B/
card: [tryboot]
card: os_prefix=slots/A/
hold: the same trial on a pristine card, held:
hold: boot: slot B -- a trial (committed is A); the watchdog holds the rollback until every service has started
hold: boot: watchdog -- off by the boot line (the emulator resets on arming); a trial cannot roll back by hardware here
hold: boot: start kds -- pid N -- /stzr /app/kds.luau
hold: kds: the kitchen display world is up on the Makeen box (aarch64, stzr under PID 1)
hold: kds: read /etc/machine -- 8 declarations rode in the image
hold: boot: kds (pid N) exited 0
hold: boot: start poste -- pid N -- /stzr /app/poste.luau
hold: poste: the counter world is up on the Makeen box, after kds
hold: poste: /data is the box's persistent partition, mounted by PID 1 before any world spoke
hold: boot: poste (pid N) exited 0
hold: boot: every service has ended -- init has nothing left to keep alive
hold: boot: --hold: the trial is held, not committed
hold: boot: --hold: no watchdog to answer here; the trial ends without a commit, the next boot is the committed slot
hold: boot: init halts the machine -- reboot(RESTART)
hold: reboot: Restarting system
card: config.txt after the held trial:
card: os_prefix=slots/A/
card: [tryboot]
card: os_prefix=slots/B/
